<title>AUSTRALIA: Commonwealth drops fixed home loan rates.</title>
<headline>Commonwealth drops fixed home loan rates.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Bank of Australia said on Friday it would reduce interest rates on a number of its fixed rate home loans and investment home loans by up to 0.25 percentage points.</p>
<p>Commonwealth's one year guaranteed rate remains unchanged at 6.49 percent while its three and four year loans will both fall by 0.25 percent when the new rates come into effect on July 21.  </p>
<p>&quot;We remain committed to providing highly competitive interest rates to home loan borrowers and this commitment is evidenced by our popular fixed rate loans which are among the lowest in the market,&quot; Commonwealth Bank's personal banking assistant general manager Adrian Cosenza said in a statement.</p>
<p>Commonwealth's new fixed rates are:</p>
<p>1 year</p>
<p>    guaranteed   6.49 percent (unchanged)</p>
<p>    1 year	 6.75 percent (from 6.89 percent)</p>
<p>    2 year	 6.99 percent (from 7.20 percent)</p>
<p>    3 year	 7.25 percent (from 7.50 percent)</p>
<p>    4 year	 7.65 percent (from 7.90 percent)</p>
<p>    5 year	 7.75 percent (from 7.95 percent)</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
